 * Proof steps:
001. AB = AC [00] & DC = DB [03] ⇒  BC ⟂ AD [09]
002. D,B,C are collinear [02] & BC ⟂ AD [09] & AB ⟂ AC [01] ⇒  ∠BAC = ∠ADB [10]
003. FD = FC [05] & FG = FC [08] & FC = FE [06] ⇒  D,G,C,E are concyclic [11]
004. D,G,C,E are concyclic [11] ⇒  ∠DGE = ∠DCE [12]
005. G,B,E are collinear [07] & D,B,C are collinear [02] & ∠DGE = ∠DCE [12] & C,A,E are collinear [04] ⇒  ∠(CA-GB) = ∠BDG [13]
006. ∠BAC = ∠ADB [10] & ∠(CA-GB) = ∠BDG [13] ⇒  ∠ABG = ∠ADG [14]
007. G,B,E are collinear [07] & ∠ABG = ∠ADG [14] ⇒  ∠BAD = ∠BGD [15]
008. ∠BAD = ∠BGD [15] ⇒  D,B,A,G are concyclic [16]
009. D,B,A,G are concyclic [16] ⇒  ∠DBG = ∠DAG [17]
010. ∠DBG = ∠DAG [17] & D,B,C are collinear [02] & G,B,E are collinear [07] & BC ⟂ AD [09] ⇒  AG ⟂ BE
